<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῡλ-ός</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>juice</i> in general, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ocell.
				2.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>in Nic.</u>
				p.81
			</span></i> P.; in various uses: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>juice of plants,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυλῶν στακτῶν εἴτε ἀνθῶν ἢ καρπῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Criti.</u>
					115a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				596b15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Col.</u>
				796a23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aud.</u>
				802a15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				6.4.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>4 Ma.</u>
				6.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>decoction,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				<u>Eup.</u>
				1.55
			</span></i>; but distd. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφέψημα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.105
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of
				<i>animal juices,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Alim.</u>
				11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Col.</u>
				794a21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>juice produced by the digestion of food, chyle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>barley-water, gruel,</i> having the barley or groats strained
			off, whereas <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτισάνη</span> was taken
			unstrained, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτισάνης χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Acut.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				297
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ephipp.
				13.6
			</span></i> (anap.): pl., <i><span class="en">
				Anaxipp.
				1.46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυμός</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i>flavour, taste,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gorg.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				7.85
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1118a28
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ διὰ χυλῶν ἡδοναί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					67
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.</u>
				3
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				p.63U.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.103K.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ὀσμὴν καὶ χρόαν καὶ χυλόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					27
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. στωμυλμάτων, φιλίας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				943
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				997
			</span></i> (anap.). (<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				11.450
			</span></i> distinguishes <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυλός</span>
			<i>juice</i> fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυμός</span>
			<i>flavour,</i> attributing this usage to Aristotle and later
			writers, whereas earlier authors used <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυμός</span> in both senses: the Mss. vary.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
